  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line. All 7 tests pass, and `python3 -m shop.demo` prints `1` (only the Gadget is left).\n\n**Root cause:** `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` filtered lines by `l.item.name` instead of `l.item.sku`. The Widget's name is `'Widget'`, so it never equalled `'sku-1'` and nothing was ever removed.\n\n**Fix:** it now filters on `l.item.sku`, the same field `Cart.add` uses to find lines.\n\nI also added a regression test, `test_remove_by_sku`, to `tests/test_pricing.py`. It builds the same cart as the demo and checks that only `sku-2` remains after the remove. There's no separate test file for the cart model, which is why it went there.",
